 ...

 &APERTURE
  LApert=T,
  File_Aperture(1)='Rad',
  Ap_Z1(1)=0.1000    , Ap_Z2(1)=0.1200,
  Ap_R(1)=1.500,
  A_xoff(1)=0.5E-3,
  File_Aperture(2)='RAD',
  Ap_Z1(2)=0.19000    , Ap_Z2(2)=0.200,
  Ap_R(2)=-50.0,
 /

 ...

Element 1: A circular aperture with 1.5 mm opening radius and 0.5 mm horizontal offset, extending from 10 cm up to 12 cm
Element 2: A beam stop (negative radius of 50 mm) at 19 cm.

 ...

 &APERTURE
  LApert=T,
  File_Aperture(1)='Scr_X',
  Ap_Z1(1)=0.1000    , Ap_Z2(1)=0.1100,
  Ap_R(1)=2.000,
  File_Aperture(2)='Scr_Y',
  Ap_Z1(2)=0.11000    , Ap_Z2(2)=0.1200,
  Ap_R(2)=3.0,
 /

 ...

Two single sided scraper forming a 90 degree angle
Element 1: A single sided planar scraper in X extending from 10 cm up to 11 cm with 2 mm opening.
Element 2: A single sided planar scraper in Y extending from 11 cm up to 12 cm with 3 mm opening.

...

 &APERTURE
  LApert=T,
  File_Aperture(1)='Col_X',
  Ap_Z1(1)=0.1000    , Ap_Z2(1)=0.1100,
  Ap_R(1)=2.000,
  File_Aperture(2)='Col_Y',
  Ap_Z1(2)=0.11000    , Ap_Z2(2)=0.1200,
  Ap_R(2)=3.0,
 /

 ...

A rectangular aperture with 4 mm x 6 mm opening
Element 1: A double sided planar collimator in X extending from 10 cm up to 11 cm with 2 mm opening.
Element 2: A double sided planar collimator in Y extending from 11 cm up to 12 cm with 3 mm opening.

...

 &APERTURE
  LApert=T,
  File_Aperture(1)='CIR',
  Ap_Z1(1)=0.0200    , Ap_Z2(1)=0.02100,
  Ap_GR(1,1)=0.000,
  Ap_GR(1,2)=0.500,
  Ap_GR(1,3)=0.600,
  Ap_GR(1,4)=0.700,
  Ap_GR(1,5)=0.800,
  Ap_GR(1,6)=0.900,
  Ap_GR(1,7)=1.000,
  Ap_GR(1,8)=1.100,
  Ap_GR(1,9)=1.200,
  Ap_GR(1,10)=1.300,
 /

...

Example of a circular grid aperture consisting of 5 rings. Longitudinal extension from 2 cm up to 2.1
cm, first ring from 0.0 to 0.5 mm, second ring from 0.6 to 0.7 mm, third ring from 0.8 to 0.9 mm
fourth ring from 1.0 to 1.1 mm, fifth ring from 1.2 to 1.3 mm.

...

 &APERTURE
  LApert=T,
  File_Aperture(1)='Geometry.dat',
 /

 ...

Circular aperture defined by the table 'Geometry.dat'. The data of the table extend from 1.0E-4 m up
to 1.0 m and form the inner contour of an rf gun cavity and a beam tube. The data table can also be
red by fieldplot and lineplot.
